# Draft. Before release: fill in given names / ORCIDs, the version and date, and the
# Zenodo DOI; when the paper is out, fill in preferred-citation's journal, volume and DOI.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lite Classify, please cite the software and the paper below."
title: "Lite Classify"
abstract: >-
  A desktop application for geographic object-based image analysis (GEOBIA) of
  ultra-high-resolution UAS orthomosaics: SLIC segmentation, object features from RGB and
  a photogrammetric DSM, class discovery with self-supervised DINOv2 context embeddings,
  Random Forest classification, and design-based accuracy assessment.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barua
    given-names: "L. D."
    affiliation: "Makiling Center for Mountain Ecosystems, College of Forestry and Natural Resources, University of the Philippines Los Baños"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leobarua/liteclassify"
url: "https://leobarua.github.io/liteclassify/"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: "1.0"
# date-released: "2026-MM-DD"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
keywords:
  - GEOBIA
  - object-based image analysis
  - unmanned aerial systems
  - SLIC superpixels
  - self-supervised vision transformer
  - Random Forest
  - accuracy assessment
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Lite Classify: an open-source geographic object-based image analysis application for ultra-high-resolution UAS orthomosaics"
